## 5. When the docs subagent returns

I check every snapshot claim against the evidence, then:

```bash
W=$R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $W grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"          # must be empty
git -C $W add -A && git -C $W commit -m "docs(wg-keepalive): snapshot ccs-it, design/plan implemented (PR #165)" -m "Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
git -C $W push -u origin chore/wg-keepalive-docs
gh pr create --head chore/wg-keepalive-docs --title "docs: close WireGuard keepalive relay" --body-file $SCRATCH/pr-body-wg-docs.md
gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch
```

I also run the project's docs-only check before the merge.

Memory: I write `wg-keepalive-relay-ccs-it.md` (type `project`) plus a `MEMORY.md` pointer. It records that the relay is live on `ccs-it` since 2026-09-28 (PR #165) and that `ccs-ops` is still pre-relay. Any traps from `wgka`'s final report go in only if they have evidence.

Backlog: `docs closed: yes`, then republish.

## 6. Cleanup (foreground)

```bash
herdr agent get wgka                                        # idle, not focused
git -C $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain # must be empty
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C $R worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C $R worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $R worktree prune
git -C $R pull
git -C $R branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $R worktree list
ps -p 48211 -o pid,lstart,command                           # confirm it is my 21:30 broker
kill 48211
```

Backlog: WG goes to `done`, then republish. I then send a second Russian status: "WireGuard keepalive relay — `done`", listing only what I verified in steps 5 and 6.

## Why

- **Acceptance is not the end.** A task is `done` only with docs closed and cleanup finished (§7, §8 stages 14–16). "Harmless" and "paperwork for later" is how a snapshot goes stale, and the RDP audio design would then be drawn against a pre-relay description of the same gateway.
- **The close-out costs the deadline nothing.** A subagent writes, I verify, and the brainstorm runs in parallel.
- **`wgka` is closed.** One tab is one task, and an unrelated next task gets a fresh tab (§4). No executor may exist for RDP audio before `brainstormed` (§10a). What `wgka` knows is in the repository, which the product advisors can read.
- **RDP audio starts at stage 0.** It is a new task, so two product advisors draft it in tabs separate from the voters. I hand over facts and design nothing.
- **"By morning" is a wish.** It waives no gate, and the full three rounds plausibly fit overnight, so nothing conflicts with a rule yet. If they do not fit, that is a change of course and the operator's poll, never a shortened brainstorm.
- **Nine hours in is a reason to write state down.** The backlog and memory are what survive my own compaction.
